#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:10
msgid "Basic Check Methodology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:12
msgid ""
"**Purpose** The basic_check methodology provides a lightweight validation"
" that ensures program outputs are generated correctly and appear "
"reasonable at first glance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:15
msgid ""
"**Scope** This methodology covers files in the test output directories "
"(``tests/.../out/`` and ``tests/.../pages/``) and certifies that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:18
msgid "The program successfully generates the expected output files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:19
msgid "The content appears reasonable and follows expected patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:20
msgid "A human has performed a basic visual inspection of the results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:22
msgid ""
"**Covered File Types** - ``.csv`` files (e.g., ``investments.csv``, "
"``.log.csv``) - ``.yaml`` files (e.g., ``investments_add_infos.yaml``) - "
"``.pkl`` files (specifically ``results.pkl``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:27
msgid "**Protocol Steps**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:29
msgid ""
"**File Generation Check**: Verify that all expected output files are "
"created by the program"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Basic Content Validation**: - Check that CSV files contain data with "
"expected columns - Verify YAML files have valid structure and contain "
"expected keys - Ensure pickle files can be loaded and contain data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:34
msgid ""
"**Human Visual Inspection**: - Quick review of output data for obvious "
"anomalies - Confirmation that data appears reasonable for the test case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:37
msgid ""
"**Cross-reference Check**: Verify that ``results.pkl`` is derived from "
"``pdf_blks`` and ``txt_blks`` inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:39
msgid ""
"**Trust Level** This methodology provides **weak certification** - it "
"indicates the program functions correctly on test data and produces "
"outputs that appear reasonable, but does not guarantee complete accuracy "
"or comprehensive data validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:42
msgid ""
"**Applicable Context** Use this methodology for routine testing and "
"development verification where comprehensive manual review is not "
"required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:46
msgid "Supported paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:48
msgid ""
"Vouching for a file under this methodology means the protocol above was "
"applied to *that file*. What that means concretely depends on what the "
"file is, so each path this methodology covers says so. All patterns are "
"relative to the root of the repository the granted file lives in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:52
msgid "``tests/formats/**/out/*.csv``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:53
msgid ""
"The tabular reference output of a format's test suite, in a **formats "
"repository** -- the files ``freeports-dev make-tests`` writes and "
"``freeports-dev test`` afterwards compares against. A basic check here "
"means the run that produced them completed, the columns are the ones "
"expected, and a person has read the values looking for obvious nonsense. "
"It includes ``.log.csv``, whose basic check is that its contents were "
"read rather than merely produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:59
msgid "``tests/formats/**/out/*.yaml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:60
msgid ""
"The non-tabular output of the same run, such as "
"``investments_add_infos.yaml``. A basic check here means the file parses,"
" carries the keys expected of it, and its values were looked at."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:63
msgid "``tests/formats/**/pages/**``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:64
msgid ""
"The per-page fixtures of the same suite: the blocks the extraction saw "
"and the result it reached for one page. A basic check here means the page"
" was classified as the fixture says, and that a person confirmed it by "
"eye against the report it came from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:70
msgid ""
"These paths mean what they say **in a formats repository** -- one with a "
"``metadata/formats.csv`` at its root, whose ``tests/formats/`` holds "
"reports and the fixtures made from them. A directory of the same name in "
"the extraction engine's own repository holds fixtures of the library "
"rather than of any format, and this methodology does not describe what "
"vouching for one of those would mean."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/validation/methodologies/basic_check.rst:76
msgid ""
"Note also that the variant level between a format and its outputs is "
"optional: both ``tests/formats/ASTERIA-EN23/out/funds.csv`` and "
"``tests/formats/ARCA-IT24/1/out/funds.csv`` are ordinary, which is why "
"the patterns above are written with ``**`` rather than with ``*``."
msgstr ""

